                <pb facs="0383" n="371" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg371"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW 1939/31399a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Standley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-21T11:00:00-04:00">September 21,
                            1943—11 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>881. At the direction of the President and in view of the military situation in
                    Italy, you are instructed to inform the Soviet Government that it is proposed to
                    send the following message to General Eisenhower, the Allied Commander in Chief
                    in the Mediterranean theater. In conveying this message to the Soviet Government
                    you should transmit a very close paraphrase:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of message printed on <ref target="#pg373">page
                    373</ref>.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
